# Allowlist: ignore everything, then opt files in explicitly.
# ROMs, extracted assets, build output and refs/ must never be committed.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
!README_MIYOO.md
!tools/
!tools/*.sh
!tools/*.py
!tools/*.c
!dev.sh
# site/screenshots.png stay untracked
!docker/
!docker/Dockerfile
# miyoo/: the Miyoo Mini release's packer inputs (from the shared Miyoo kit): game.json, the packer, its templates
!miyoo/
!miyoo/game.json
!miyoo/icon.png
!miyoo/icon.svg
!miyoo/tools/
!miyoo/tools/*.py
!miyoo/templates/
!miyoo/templates/*
# The port tree: code only. port/decomp = JRickey/ssb-decomp-re @ 2898d4d9
# minus src/relocData (the ROM's data as C), ovl8 and db code; port/hh = our
# layer (MK64/OoT kit + C from BattleShip, MIT). build/ is never tracked.
!port/
!port/**
port/build/
port/**/*.o
port/**/*.d
# Belt and braces: never track ROM images or extracted data even if allowlisted above.
*.z64
*.n64
*.v64
*.rom
*.bin
*.o2r
*.otr
*.zip

# desktop save dir (holds the ROM slice): never commit
port/ssb64_data/
# macOS Finder files (the port/** allowlist above would otherwise pick them up)
.DS_Store
# the Miyoo64 repository's docs
!SETTINGS.md
